# Web design fidelity

Before building or restyling Angular UI, read **docs/design/stitch/** (canonical) and **docs/web/implementation.md** §4 / §6.6. Copy missing Stitch exports from `mobile/designs/stitch_vaxiil_app_design/` into `docs/design/stitch/` first.

## Source of truth

- Open the matching screen’s `code.html` + `screen.png` before implementing.
- Tokens: Verdant Pulse (`web/src/styles/tokens.css`); do not invent alternate palettes or layouts.
- Adapt phone artboards into shells (consumer top nav / business sidebar). Do not stretch phone chrome for management screens.

## Page vs modal (Flutter `modalOnWide` parity)

Breakpoint: **768** (`md`). Wide = centered dismissible panel (max-width ~720) over dimmed barrier; compact = full page. Match [`mobile/lib/core/router/app_router.dart`](mobile/lib/core/router/app_router.dart) `modalOnWide: true`.

**Modal on wide:** service detail, book schedule, booking detail, booking confirmation, payment return, edit profile, privacy settings, KYC; business setup, business service create/edit, business booking detail.

**Always pages:** discover, services list, bookings list, profile, messages; business companies list, hub, services list, bookings inbox, team, analytics, settings; auth onboarding/login/register.

Confirm/delete prompts stay small dialogs on all breakpoints.

## Responsive

- Breakpoints: **768** (`md`) / **1024** (`lg`), aligned with Flutter.
- Business/staff: `BusinessManageShell` / `PlatformStaffShell` — desktop-first tables + filters, not consumer bottom-nav.

## i18n

User-facing chrome must be translated (en/fr). See [.cursor/rules/i18n.mdc](i18n.mdc).
